  "result": "All completion tests pass. \n\n## Summary\n\nThe bug: `_TUPLE_PARAM_COMPLETE=zsh_source ...` output was emitted via `click.echo(comp.source())`, writing the generated shell script as a `str` through click's text-mode output stream. Python's `io.TextIOWrapper` (used for stdout there) translates embedded `\\n` to `os.linesep` on write when no explicit `newline` is set. On Windows-hosted shells (e.g., msys2 zsh via Git-for-Windows Python), this turns `\\n` into `\\r\\n`, so tokens like `then` become `then\\r` \u2014 no longer a recognized shell keyword \u2014 breaking the `if/elif/fi` control structure and producing `parse error near 'elif'`.\n\n**Fix** (`src/click/shell_completion.py`): encode the generated script/completions to `bytes` before calling `echo`, since `echo` writes `bytes`/`bytearray` directly to the underlying binary stream, bypassing the text-mode newline translation and preserving literal `\\n` line endings regardless of platform.\n\nRan `tests/test_shell_completion.py` and all completion-related tests (`-k \"complet\"`) \u2014 all 53 pass.",
